# 7. GAME THREE — THE MARKET

Working title: "Market Missions."

## Core concept

The player manages a small market stall and must fulfill requests expressed in Arabic.

The task is to understand a customer and select the correct products and quantities.

Example:

"أَعْطِنِي تُفَّاحَتَيْنِ حَمْرَاوَيْنِ."

The learner must select two red apples, place them in a basket, and complete the delivery.

Use Arabic examples that have been checked for grammatical correctness and naturalness.

## Progression

### Stage 1 — Names

Identify familiar products.

### Stage 2 — Colors

Match Arabic color words to products.

### Stage 3 — Quantity

Understand numbers and the quantities required.

### Stage 4 — Descriptions

Understand the difference between red and green, large and small, or other appropriate vocabulary.

### Stage 5 — Simple requests

Fulfill complete Arabic instructions.

### Stage 6 — More complex orders

Combine quantities, descriptions, objects, and simple contextual information.

Where appropriate, introduce singular, dual, and plural distinctions, along with adjective agreement. Do not introduce complex grammar before learners have the appropriate foundations.

## Gameplay

Allow players to:

- Select objects.
- Place them in a basket.
- Remove incorrect objects.
- Submit an order.
- Receive corrective feedback.
- Retry the order.
- Unlock new product collections after demonstrating understanding.

Do not make purchases, real payments, or financial transactions part of the MVP.

Use the market purely as an educational simulation.

