# 8. GAME FOUR — THE SENTENCE BRIDGE

## Core concept

Create a puzzle environment in which a character cannot proceed until the learner constructs a meaningful Arabic sentence.

The learner drags or selects word tiles, arranges them into a sentence, and then checks the meaning.

Example:

"يَقْرَأُ الْوَلَدُ الْكِتَابَ."

The player builds the sentence using the provided word tiles.

When the answer is accepted, a path or bridge becomes available and the player continues.

## Requirements

- Support touch and mouse interaction.
- Provide a way to undo and rearrange tiles.
- Give contextual hints.
- Explain why the accepted sentence works.
- Support valid alternative answers when appropriate.
- Use a validated answer model instead of hard-coded assumptions about a single word order.

The visual bridge is a metaphor for sentence construction, not a reward attached to religious merit.

Progress from simple patterns to pronouns, prepositions, sentence relationships, and selected intermediate structures.

