# 10. GAME SIX — THE WORD DETECTIVE

## Core concept

Create an investigative word-learning game that helps advanced beginners and intermediate learners notice relationships between Arabic word forms.

The learner receives clues, investigates related words, and builds a visual family of words.

For example, a validated set may explore:

- كَتَبَ
- كِتَاب
- كَاتِب
- مَكْتُوب

The task is not simply to match each word to a translation.

The learner should understand that these forms have relationships while recognizing that grammatical form, meaning, and contextual usage are not identical.

## Requirements

- Show verified lexical or morphological relationships.
- Distinguish roots, stems, derived forms, and inflections where applicable.
- Allow exploration of words through visual nodes and connections.
- Ask learners to predict or identify relationships.
- Reveal explanations when the learner needs help.
- Provide examples in context.
- Reuse vocabulary already learned where possible.

Do not invent Arabic roots or assume that visually similar words necessarily share a useful semantic relationship.

Use a validated lexical dataset and expose source information to learners when appropriate.

Do not automatically label every visually related word as having the same underlying meaning.

