# 11. GAME SEVEN — QURANIC DISCOVERY

This experience connects the game world to the core purpose of the platform: understanding Quranic Arabic.

It must be implemented with stronger content verification and a more restrained visual style than the ordinary games.

## Core experience

The learner opens a selected, verified Quranic passage.

They can:

1. Listen to an authorized recitation when available.
2. Select an individual word.
3. Explore a reviewed lexical explanation.
4. Examine a relevant grammatical relationship.
5. View an accurately attributed translation.
6. Complete a language-comprehension activity.
7. Review previously learned vocabulary in later sessions.

## Design restrictions

- Do not use Quranic verses as collectible coins, projectiles, platforms, obstacles, or objects that are jumped on.
- Do not use arcade-style effects that trivialize the sacred text.
- Do not assign spiritual rewards, blessings, or religious merit points.
- Do not present gameplay results as a measure of a person's faith or piety.
- Do not generate or invent Quranic interpretations.
- Do not confuse a lexical gloss with tafsir.
- Do not represent a learner's personal reflection as authoritative interpretation.

Reward educational effort and demonstrated language comprehension, not the sacred status of the text itself.

The presentation should be beautiful, calm, accurate, and respectful.

## Content verification

Use only Quranic text, translations, references, audio, and tafsir content from identified sources with appropriate licensing and editorial review.

Store source attribution with each relevant content item.

If no verified Quranic content exists for a planned activity, do not invent some to populate the game.

Use clearly labeled general Arabic demonstration content until valid educational material has been reviewed.

