# 13. SPACED REPETITION AND SKILL TRANSFER

Implement a reusable review system.

When the learner makes repeated mistakes with a word or phrase:

- Record the specific vocabulary or skill involved.
- Offer an appropriate review activity.
- Reintroduce the word in a different game.
- Schedule a later recall opportunity.
- Track whether performance improves.

Allow users to revise and delete their learning history where appropriate.

The system should adapt to what the learner actually finds difficult.

Do not rely exclusively on the same question or image to measure retention.

For example, a learner who understands "تَحْتَ" in the Scene Lab should later encounter the term in a new scene or direction task.

Distinguish recall from recognition.

Avoid generating enormous numbers of repetitive tasks just to increase session duration.

