# 20. PERFORMANCE AND STABILITY

Optimize the world and game rendering for common mobile devices.

Requirements:

- Load only the resources needed for the current activity.
- Avoid giant image assets where smaller sprites or vectors suffice.
- Avoid unnecessary animation loops when the game is idle or paused.
- Prevent uncontrolled timers and duplicated keyboard handlers.
- Clean up event listeners when leaving a game.
- Maintain stable movement and collision behavior.
- Avoid blocking the entire application when one game fails to initialize.
- Preserve learner progress during recoverable errors.
- Show meaningful loading and error states.

Do not let decorative effects compromise movement responsiveness.

Keep the initial page lightweight and load interactive worlds progressively.

