# 21. EDUCATIONAL CONTENT AND QUALITY CONTROL

All educational examples must be reviewed for linguistic correctness.

This includes:

- Arabic spelling.
- Diacritics.
- Grammatical agreement.
- Word order.
- Natural imperatives.
- Vocabulary meanings.
- Morphological relationships.
- Contextual usage.
- Indonesian and Malaysian explanations.

Create a content validation workflow.

Possible status values include:

- Draft.
- Needs linguistic review.
- Needs source verification.
- Approved for publication.

Do not treat source labels in the code as evidence of actual human review.

Keep unapproved educational data out of production learning paths or label it clearly as demonstration material.

For Quranic data:

- Never invent verses or Quranic wording.
- Never fabricate references or translations.
- Verify verse boundaries and the alignment of words with their source text.
- Attribute translations and tafsir.
- Check audio licenses.
- Separate language teaching from authoritative religious interpretation.
- Have qualified reviewers approve religious instructional content before publication.

AI may assist with draft generation, but must not be treated as an authoritative validator of religious claims.

