# 22. PRODUCT ANALYTICS AND LEARNING OUTCOMES

Track the performance of the educational experience, not merely engagement.

Where analytics are configured and appropriately consented to, useful events may include:

- Game started.
- Game completed.
- Level restarted.
- Task answered correctly.
- Task answered incorrectly.
- Hint requested.
- Previously learned word recalled.
- Review session completed.
- Learner returned for another session.

Collect only necessary data.

Do not publicly expose private learning histories.

Do not collect sensitive personal information without a justified need and appropriate protections.

The main learning metrics should include:

- First-session completion.
- Ability to understand instructions after multiple exposures.
- Recall after a delay.
- Transfer to a different scene or game.
- Drop-off points.
- Voluntary return and review.

Higher play time or more clicks do not automatically mean better learning.

Design the code so these metrics can be connected to a real analytics provider later without rebuilding the educational architecture.

