# FINAL DIRECTIVE

The goal is not to make an ordinary Arabic website look more playful.

The goal is to change how the learner experiences Arabic.

Build an interconnected educational world where Arabic words become actions, actions become meaningful experiences, and previously learned vocabulary is repeatedly applied in new situations.

Make the Neighborhood, Market, Scene Lab, Sentence Bridge, narrative game, Word Detective, and Quranic Discovery environment feel like parts of one coherent learning system.

Prioritize a small number of truly playable, polished, educationally sound games over a large collection of superficial features.

Preserve the existing product, implement the features in the actual repository, test them, and report honestly what works.

Do not stop at writing a plan. Start by inspecting the codebase and then implement the highest-priority complete vertical slice.
